Replay ordinary and projected LIN weight placement on FlashProve's two exact-match
key proofs. The diagnostic obtains the genuine second-chain events from the regular
key verifier. It changes the third FOLD round after transcript authentication and
runs the same FV.custom verifier with both weight representations. This isolates
the algebraic checks from failures in message hashing or Merkle authentication.

From a checkout containing this patch, create a separate worktree at the revision
under review. Use the repository's normal native CPU build prerequisites.

    git worktree add --detach build/lin-replay 9d00a32cb967a124159b562563cc7c5a9673bbcd
    git -C build/lin-replay apply ../../research/spikes/request/lin-transcript-check.patch
    cd build/lin-replay
    make bootstrap upstream plans build/key-stage
    for fixture in accepted-proof full-size; do
      dir=.upstream/FlashProve/examples/$fixture
      build/key-stage build/plans "$dir/config" "$dir/ivk/key.bin" || exit 1
    done

Each command must exit zero and print eligible True before the cases. The next
columns are the case number, the ordinary verdict and the projected verdict.

    7 False False    both coefficients replaced by zero
    6 False False    gamma replaced by a different cubic field element
    5 False False    round duplicated
    4 False False    round removed
    3 False False    round given an unknown name
    2 False False    coefficient message truncated to zero bytes
    1 False False    low bit of the first coefficient flipped
    0 True True      original authenticated trace

The descriptions at the right are explanatory. The last printed line is the
regular key-transcript record. Both fixtures passed these 16 comparisons in a
native Linux run. This experiment tests those rounds on those two proofs.

